#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Write logs from a managed workflow, report errors that your local notebook "
"can read, and save partial work when a job is canceled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs and handle errors"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore levelname */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs and handle errors {#write-logs-and-handle-errors}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* <Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Placeholder content\">\n"
"- **Errors from custom workflows.** A managed workflow stores a structured error for a custom workflow only when the workflow calls `send_error()`. If custom workflows get the same top-level handler as Catalog Functions, remove the handler from [Best practice: report errors with send_error()](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error).\n"
"- **Time after cancel.** Confirm how long a job can run after `SIGTERM` before the managed workflow stops it.\n"
"</Admonition> */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set up your workflow code to write logs, report errors to your local "
"notebook, and save partial work when a job is canceled. To read these "
"outputs from your local notebook, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-"
"managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| In the workflow | In your local notebook |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Write with a logger from the `logging` module, or call `print()`. | `job.logs()` returns the lines. |\n"
"| Raise an exception, or exit with a nonzero code. | `job.status()` returns `ERROR`, and `job.logs()` shows the traceback. |\n"
"| Call `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` and `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` return the code, message, and details. |\n"
"| Call `save_result()` in a `SIGTERM` handler. | `job.result()` returns the partial result of a canceled job. |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs {#write-logs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes "
"to the job's logs. Read the logs with `job.logs()` while the job runs or "
"after it ends.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up a logger {#set-up-a-logger}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `logging` module from the Python standard library. "
"`logging.basicConfig()` writes to standard error, which reaches the logs "
"without delay. The format in the following example adds a timestamp to each "
"line:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`level=logging.WARNING` hides `INFO` messages from other packages, and "
"`logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` keeps `INFO` messages for your own logger. "
"`qiskit_ibm_runtime` sets its own level with the "
"`QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`print()` also reaches the logs, but standard output is buffered, so printed"
" lines might not appear until the job ends. If you use `print()`, pass "
"`flush=True`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: get_logger() from qiskit_serverless adds a [PUBLIC] prefix that "
"Functions uses to split provider and user logs for Catalog Functions; custom"
" workflow logs strip it. Tested with 0.37.0: its lines have no timestamp, "
"and logger.exception() and exc_info=True drop the traceback (PrefixFormatter"
" builds new records with exc_info=None). Confirm whether to recommend the "
"standard logging module for custom workflows, or to fix get_logger(). */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set the log level for each run {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To debug one run without changing the code, pass the log level as an "
"argument:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, set the level of your logger from the argument:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the workflow has an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-"
"and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), declare "
"`log_level` in it, for example as `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", "
"\"WARNING\"]}`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: decide what to log {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Log enough to reconstruct a run from its logs:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**At the start, log what the run received.** Log the backend name, the "
"number of circuits, and the other settings that change between runs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Log the start and end of each stage.** Use fixed messages that you can "
"search for.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Log iterations at a fixed interval.** For example, log a line such as "
"`iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` every 10 iterations, instead of every "
"iteration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Log exceptions with `logger.exception()` inside an `except` block.** The "
"line includes the full traceback, even if the workflow recovers from the "
"error.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Turn off progress bars.** The logs store each refresh of a progress bar, "
"such as one from `tqdm`, as a separate line. Pass `disable=True` to `tqdm`, "
"or log at an interval instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Keep the logs small.** Do not log large data, such as every shot. A "
"managed workflow keeps only the newest 50 MB of logs for each job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Use the words \"error\" and \"exception\" only in messages about "
"failures.** If a failed job did not [report its error](#best-practice-"
"report-errors-with-send_error), the exception that `job.result()` raises "
"contains only the log lines that include these words.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Best practice: report errors with send_error() {#best-practice-report-"
"errors-with-send_error}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status,"
" and the traceback goes to the logs. A managed workflow does not store the "
"error, even for a `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` returns `{}`, and"
" the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that "
"include `error` or `exception`. Checks of argument types and ranges belong "
"in an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-"
"practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), which rejects a bad run before "
"the job starts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Report every error that stops the workflow with `send_error()`, so that your"
" local notebook gets a short error with a code and details:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` with the same text.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To enable this, raise `ServerlessError` where the error happens, and wrap "
"the code of your entrypoint in a `try` block that sends any error with "
"`send_error()`. A workflow adds this handler to Catalog Functions, but not "
"to managed workflows:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Raise the error again.** The final `raise` keeps the traceback in the logs"
" and ends the job with the `ERROR` status.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Subclass `ServerlessError` to name a group of errors.** The handler sends "
"the name of the class, such as `InputError`, as the `exception` field.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Other exceptions also reach the handler.** They get the code `1`, and "
"their `repr()` becomes the message, such as `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: custom (user) workflows run their entrypoint directly through "
"fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py (fleets_runner.py "
"_upload_custom_image_entrypoint). Only provider jobs get the main.tmpl "
"handler, which calls send_error() for an uncaught exception. Should custom "
"jobs get the same handler? Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0: a raised "
"ServerlessError creates no ERROR event, and error_message() returns {}. "
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Report a problem and continue {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`send_error()` does not stop the workflow or change its status, so you can "
"also report problems that the workflow recovers from, such as each circuit "
"that it skips:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns every error that the workflow reported,"
" including the errors of a job that ended with the `DONE` status. See [Find "
"the cause of an error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-"
"error).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Pass numbers and strings in `args`.** `error_message()` shows only the "
"first item of a list.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Check the return value.** If a workflow cannot store the error, for "
"example because the code runs outside a job, `send_error()` writes the error"
" to the logs and returns `False`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: confirm which error codes user workflows should use. Catalog "
"Function codes come from the IBM Quantum error code registry, which might "
"not apply to user workflows. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up when a job is canceled {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you cancel a job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint, "
"uploads the final logs, and shuts down the environment. Without a handler, "
"Python stops immediately, and `finally` blocks do not run. The workflow also"
" tries to cancel the QPU jobs and sessions that the workflow started with "
"`get_runtime_service()`. See [Cancel linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-"
"quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To keep partial work, register a handler for `SIGTERM`. Your local notebook "
"then gets the partial result from a canceled job:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, add the handler at the start of your entrypoint:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`sys.exit()` in the handler raises `SystemExit` in the code that is running,"
" so `finally` blocks run before the script ends. The job still ends with the"
" `CANCELED` status.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keep the handler short, because the workflow shuts down the environment soon"
" after `SIGTERM`. For long runs, also save checkpoints, so that a later run "
"can resume after a job fails or reaches the 24-hour limit. See [Best "
"practice: checkpoint long jobs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-"
"workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: confirm the time between SIGTERM and shutdown. The cancel is a "
"Code Engine hard stop (fleets/handler.py cancel_job, "
"cancel_processing_tasks=True), and the repo sets no grace period. Tested "
"with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0, the real fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py, and "
"docker stop: the handler runs, save_result() writes the result, and result()"
" on a CANCELED job returns it (the result endpoint does not check the "
"status). Confirm on Fleets that a result written in the handler reaches "
"storage before the hard stop. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr ""

